@page "/disclosure"

<PageTitle>Progressive disclosure</PageTitle>
<h1>Progressive disclosure</h1>
<p>This page shows progressive disclosure (which messages a form shows, and when) on fields that come and go. A submit shows a message only for a field on screen, so the error of a field you have hidden stays out of the form.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "TravelRequest.cs", "Disclosure.razor", "Disclosure.razor.cs" })">
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Click <strong>Show traveler details</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Traveler name</strong> appears with an asterisk and no message.</div></li>
            <li>Type a name into <strong>Traveler name</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Traveler name</strong> turns green.</div></li>
            <li>Clear <strong>Traveler name</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Traveler name is required", with no submit pressed.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Hide traveler details</strong>, then click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> messages for <strong>Destination</strong> and the accommodation question; <strong>Traveler name</strong>'s error appears only in the "Suppressed-issue diagnostic" list.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> A submit shows a message only where its field is on screen.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Show traveler details</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Traveler name</strong> comes back, still empty, with no message.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> Once hidden, a field stops counting as changed; it waits for an edit or submit.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Traveler name is required" under the field and in the error summary, and the diagnostic list empties.</div></li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Yes</strong> for the accommodation question.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> its message clears, and <strong>Type</strong> appears with no message.</div></li>
            <li>Pick <strong>Accessible</strong> under <strong>Type</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Special requirements</strong> appears, empty, with no message and no asterisk.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> Its rule applies only under a condition, which the asterisk cannot judge.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Describe the special requirements" under the box and in the error summary.</div></li>
            <li>Fill in <strong>Destination</strong>, <strong>Traveler name</strong> and <strong>Special requirements</strong>, then click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Submitted" in the status line.</div></li>
            <li>Under <strong>Without a summary</strong>, click <strong>Request trip</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "The form cannot be submitted because information that is not currently displayed is invalid." at the top of that form.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Show trip details</strong>, then click <strong>Request trip</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> three messages under the fields, and the message at the top clears.</div></li>
            <li>Fill in <strong>Destination</strong> and <strong>Traveler name</strong>, choose <strong>No</strong>, and click <strong>Request trip</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Submitted" in that form's status line.</div></li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Destination</strong>: required.</li>
            <li><strong>Traveler name</strong>: required, even while its section is hidden.</li>
            <li><strong>The accommodation question</strong>: required.</li>
            <li><strong>Type</strong>: required when you answer <strong>Yes</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Special requirements</strong>: required when <strong>Type</strong> is <strong>Accessible</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Without a summary</strong>: the same validator, on a form with only <strong>Destination</strong>, <strong>Traveler name</strong> and the question.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <HowItWorks>
        <p>The page hides fields in two ways. The traveler details hide behind a button, while <strong>Traveler name</strong>'s rule applies whether they show or not. The accommodation fields appear as you answer, and each of their rules carries a <code>When</code> condition (FluentValidation's condition on a rule) matching the answer that shows its field.</p>
        <p>At a submit, a field's message shows only if the field is on screen. A collapsed section cannot show a message, so the submit suppresses (sets aside) the error of a failing field inside it. The "Suppressed-issue diagnostic" list below the form shows each one, and nothing else on the page shows that error. The page fills the list from its <code>SuppressedIssueDiagnostic</code> callback.</p>
        <p>A field that leaves the page stops counting as changed, even if you edited it before. So when it comes back, it stays quiet until you change it again (its message then appears at once) or a submit runs with it showing.</p>
        <p>As you edit, a field you have changed shows its own messages, with no submit needed. Showing a field is not changing it, so a field that appears stays quiet until you change it or press <strong>Submit</strong>. A submit shows every failing field on screen, changed or not.</p>
        <p>The accommodation question speaks only at a submit. Answering it is the only way to change it, and any answer satisfies it.</p>
        <p>The <code>When</code> conditions on the accommodation rules match what the page shows. <strong>Type</strong> shows when you answer <strong>Yes</strong>, and its rule applies only then. <strong>Special requirements</strong> and its rule follow <strong>Accessible</strong> the same way. So in the first form these rules never fail for a field that is off the screen, and never put an error in the diagnostic list. That is the pattern for an ordinary section that depends on the data.</p>
        <p>The asterisks come from the validator. Each is a <code>FormidableRequiredIndicator</code> (the component that draws the mark), placed where the page puts it. <strong>Destination</strong>'s and <strong>Traveler name</strong>'s asterisks sit inside their labels.</p>
        <p>The accommodation question's asterisk sits in the group's <code>&lt;legend&gt;</code>, outside every <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> and outside the <code>FormidableField</code> that wraps the radios. (<code>FormidableField</code> is the component that ties the page's own radio buttons to the field.) It goes there because the two labels name the options, Yes and No, not the question.</p>
        <p>Placement is markup position and nothing else: the component asks the form and its own <code>For</code>, and reads nothing from what surrounds it.</p>
        <p><strong>Type</strong> and <strong>Special requirements</strong> carry no mark, because their rules apply only under a condition. The indicator reads the rules alone, without the form's data, so it cannot tell whether a condition holds. It draws nothing rather than claim a demand it cannot check.</p>
        <p>Every asterisk is <code>aria-hidden</code>, so no label or legend reads a star aloud. The inputs carry <code>aria-required</code> instead, the two radios included: this page writes it on the radios by hand, the way Formidable's own inputs, such as <code>FormidableInputText</code>, write it for themselves.</p>
        <p>When a submit is blocked and every failing field is hidden, the form adds a message about itself: "The form cannot be submitted because information that is not currently displayed is invalid." The error summary is only one of the places it shows. The <strong>Without a summary</strong> form has no <code>FormidableSummary</code>, so a <code>FormidableModelMessage</code> (a list for messages about the form rather than a field) shows it instead.</p>
    </HowItWorks>
    <Demo>
        <FormidableForm Model="_request" Options="_options" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid"
                        @ref="_form">
            <div class="summary-slot">
                <FormidableSummary />
            </div>

            <div class="field"><label>Destination <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _request.Destination" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_request.Destination" /></label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _request.Destination" /></div>

            <p>
                <button type="button"
                        @onclick="() => _showDetails = !_showDetails">
                    @(_showDetails ? "Hide" : "Show") traveler details
                </button>
            </p>
            @if (_showDetails)
            {
                <div class="field">
                    <label>Traveler name <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _request.TravelerName" />
                        <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_request.TravelerName" /></label>
                    <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _request.TravelerName" />
                </div>
            }

            <fieldset>
                <legend>Do you need accommodation? <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _request.NeedsAccommodation" /></legend>
                <FormidableField For="() => _request.NeedsAccommodation" Context="field">
                    <label><input type="radio" name="needs" id="@field.ElementId"
                                  aria-invalid="@(field.AriaInvalid ? "true" : null)"
                                  aria-describedby="@field.AriaDescribedBy"
                                  aria-required="@(field.Requirement == FieldRequirement.Required ? "true" : null)"
                                  checked="@(_request.NeedsAccommodation == true)"
                                  @onchange="() => SetNeeds(true, field)" /> Yes</label>
                    <label><input type="radio" name="needs"
                                  aria-required="@(field.Requirement == FieldRequirement.Required ? "true" : null)"
                                  checked="@(_request.NeedsAccommodation == false)"
                                  @onchange="() => SetNeeds(false, field)" /> No</label>
                </FormidableField>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _request.NeedsAccommodation" />
            </fieldset>

            @if (_request.NeedsAccommodation == true)
            {
                <fieldset>
                    <legend>Accommodation</legend>
                    <FormidableField For="() => _request.AccommodationType" Context="field">
                        <label>Type <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _request.AccommodationType" />
                            <select id="@field.ElementId" class="@field.CssClass"
                                    aria-invalid="@(field.AriaInvalid ? "true" : null)"
                                    aria-describedby="@field.AriaDescribedBy"
                                    value="@_request.AccommodationType"
                                    @onchange="args => OnTypeChanged(args, field)">
                                <option value="">Choose…</option>
                                <option>Hotel</option>
                                <option>Serviced apartment</option>
                                <option>Accessible</option>
                            </select>
                        </label>
                    </FormidableField>
                    <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _request.AccommodationType" />

                    @if (_request.AccommodationType == "Accessible")
                    {
                        <div class="field">
                            <label>Special requirements <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _request.SpecialRequirements" />
                                <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_request.SpecialRequirements" /></label>
                            <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _request.SpecialRequirements" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </fieldset>
            }

            <div class="actions"><button type="button" class="primary" @onclick="Submit">Submit</button></div>
        </FormidableForm>

        <p role="status">@_status</p>
        <p><small>Use the <strong>Submit</strong> button rather than pressing Enter: the browser's implicit submit on Enter skips this page's clearing of the diagnostic list below.</small></p>

        <h2>Suppressed-issue diagnostic</h2>
        <p><small>The issues the form above suppressed at its most recent submit. A submit that shows every failing field leaves it empty.</small></p>
        <ul>
            @foreach (var message in _suppressed)
            {
                <li>@message</li>
            }
        </ul>

        <section id="inline-only-variant" class="form-card">
            <h2>Without a summary</h2>
            <p>This form renders no <code>FormidableSummary</code>. A <code>FormidableModelMessage</code> at its top, a
                persistent list for messages about the form itself, stays empty until the form has something to say.</p>

            <FormidableForm Model="_inlineRequest" Options="_inlineOptions"
                            OnValidSubmit="HandleInlineValid">
                <FormidableModelMessage />

                <p>
                    <button type="button" @onclick="() => _showInlineSection = !_showInlineSection">
                        @(_showInlineSection ? "Hide" : "Show") trip details
                    </button>
                </p>
                @if (_showInlineSection)
                {
                    <div class="field"><label>Destination <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _inlineRequest.Destination" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_inlineRequest.Destination" /></label>
                        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _inlineRequest.Destination" /></div>

                    <div class="field"><label>Traveler name <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _inlineRequest.TravelerName" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_inlineRequest.TravelerName" /></label>
                        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _inlineRequest.TravelerName" /></div>

                    <fieldset>
                        <legend>Do you need accommodation? <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _inlineRequest.NeedsAccommodation" /></legend>
                        <FormidableField For="() => _inlineRequest.NeedsAccommodation" Context="field">
                            <label><input type="radio" name="inline-needs" id="@field.ElementId"
                                          aria-invalid="@(field.AriaInvalid ? "true" : null)"
                                          aria-describedby="@field.AriaDescribedBy"
                                          aria-required="@(field.Requirement == FieldRequirement.Required ? "true" : null)"
                                          checked="@(_inlineRequest.NeedsAccommodation == true)"
                                          @onchange="() => SetInlineNeeds(true, field)" /> Yes</label>
                            <label><input type="radio" name="inline-needs"
                                          aria-required="@(field.Requirement == FieldRequirement.Required ? "true" : null)"
                                          checked="@(_inlineRequest.NeedsAccommodation == false)"
                                          @onchange="() => SetInlineNeeds(false, field)" /> No</label>
                        </FormidableField>
                        <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _inlineRequest.NeedsAccommodation" />
                    </fieldset>
                }

                <div class="actions"><button type="submit" class="primary">Request trip</button></div>
            </FormidableForm>

            <p role="status">@_inlineStatus</p>
        </section>
    </Demo>
</TeachingPanel>
